      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've wanted this too.\n\nI frequently will want to be able to see an individual user's avatar, but don't want to change my settings for the entire instance. So I often end up making an exception for that user by using \"show avatar\", but I then have to manually turn it off again later, at the risk of them leaving or me forgetting to do so. \n\nWhich results in a steadily growing list of \"shown avatars\" which are bypassing my settings, and require this little ritual of periodically scanning a room of people that need to be reverted to safety settings.\n\nFor sake of UI clarity - \n\nOne way to do this without further cluttering the UI, could perhaps be that when \"show avatar\" is selected, it would pop up up a secondary window with two buttons. \"Always show avatar?\" or \"Temporarily show avatar?\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
